what is going on everybody welcome back  to the cosmic wonder i'm your host  warren thompson and i just got out of  the mandalorian panel here at star wars  celebration in anaheim california they  showed us footage of the ahsoka series  which was so unexpected and they also  showed us footage for the mandalorian  season three now on thursday they  already showed us this footage but they  added an additional 30 to 45 seconds of  new footage so if you heard a  description of the mandalorian season 3  trailer or footage this is actually  going to be a bit more than what you've  heard before they didn't technically  call it a trailer it looked like a  trailer probably what they'll use as a  trailer but regardless i'm going to tell  you exactly what i saw obviously there  are no recording devices allowed when  the presentation is up so we don't link  it online but we can tell you exactly  what we saw so here's my description of  the ahsoka footage that we saw in the  mandalorian season 3 footage that we saw  which i believe  is  hands down one of the best things to  come from star wars it blew me away it  was fantastic so if you love star wars  if you love marvel if you love all  superhero stuff be sure to subscribe and  hit that bell so you don't miss out on  any of the latest videos alright so  starting with the ahsoka footage that we  saw they didn't show us much the clip  was only about 35 seconds long but what  they did show us the non-filler stuff  was pretty cool the first thing that we  see is ship doors opening up and it  reveals the bridge of the ghost we then  see hera from behind walk onto the  bridge and right behind her is ahsoka  walking onto the bridge as well then it  fades to black then it shows us more of  a ship and then it shows us somebody  sitting down they have their arm on a  table and their hand is out reaching for  a cup trying to use the force to bring  it to them now no one was actually shown  here it was just the arm of the person  but i know it wasn't ahsoka because i  remember that the hand and the arm  weren't orange so this person is a  mystery as of right now they then show a  droid and i don't believe i've seen this  droid in clone wars or rebels or  anywhere before so i'm gonna say it's a  new droid and he's only shown very very  briefly but here's where things get  pretty interesting we see ahsoka and she  has her hood on then she takes her hood  off and she's looking at somebody she  then tilts her head forward and closes  her eyes almost kind of like she's  bowing at somebody or saying hello but  it definitely looks like it's a sign of  respect that she's doing so i'm  wondering who exactly this could be  we've already had a crossover between  ahsoka and luke in boba fett so really a  lot of things are possible here and  here's where it gets even more  interesting after the title card ahsoka  shows we see a mural in the mural we see  hera ezra sabine wren zeb and kanan this  of course is sabine wren's mural and to  my knowledge from what i saw it is the  exact same one from rebels but as  they're showing the mural we see  somebody come up who is staring at it  and this person is sabine wren and they  did announce that sabine wren is going  to be played by natasha luis bordizzo so  super exciting news there and that's  pretty much all that they showed us in  the ahsoka footage just some footage put  together for the fans at star wars  celebration but definitely a big big  teaser with a lot of hints of some  awesome things to come now as far as the  mandalorian season 3 footage we actually  saw this trailer twice today so i've  seen it three times now once on thursday  and twice today with the extended  footage and i made sure to make some  notes immediately after i saw it so the  beginning is pretty much the same as the  trailer they showed us on thursday and  it opens up with the mandalorian flute  theme plane we then see the mandalorian  walking through what looks to be  destruction and based off of what they  showed us in this trailer this is  probably mandalore and he's kind of  walking through the destruction after  the night of a thousand tears and then  we hear the armorer speak and this is  what she says she says you have removed  your helmet what's worse is that you did  so of your own free will and after she  says that it shows footage of grogu and  that's kind of to show us why he removed  his helmet but she continues to say you  are no longer a mandalorian she then  says redemption is no longer possible  for you since the destruction of our  homeworld we then cut to a scene of the  mandalorian going up to bogatan who  seems to be sitting on some type of a  throne we have never seen this room  before and she said something along the  lines of you and your people gave them  mandalore where were you then and i  believe she actually calls them his cult  i think she says you and your cult so  she's pretty bitter she's pretty pissed  off and you can tell that there's just a  ton of tension between her and den then  it looks like the mandalorian returns to  navarro because there he sees grief and  grief karga looks like he is doing  extremely well for himself and when  grief sees him he laughs and he says i  heard you were back but i didn't believe  it and greets him very warmly and very  welcoming then we hear the mandalorian  talk and he says i'm going to mandalore  to be forgiven for my transgressions i  believe he's talking to bogotan and it  actually looks like maybe she's going to  help him maybe she has ulterior motives  but it does look like she is helping him  and we see her kind of in like a cave  where she shoots the top of the cave and  it creates a hole and kind of the  ceiling just falls down and when it  falls she turns and she looks at grogu  and she said did you think your dad was  the only mandalorian and from here we  just get a ton of footage and this  footage is just completely action packed  we see it both on planets and off  planets in space we see a starship fight  in an asteroid field we see a star  destroyer we see a ton of mandalorians  coming together and fighting together  and i mean a lot in the footage we saw  alone there were probably about 20  different mandalorians that we see and  then at the very end after all of this  epic footage which is just a ton of  action we actually see  mandalore we see it in the ruins that  are left of it but it was so insane to  actually see mandalore and that was it  it was actually about i would say  probably close to three minutes long  probably like two minutes and 40 seconds  and again they didn't call it the  trailer but it is a trailer it's a full  trailer put together just like a trailer  typically is and i'm hoping this is  released pretty soon they did confirm  that the mandalorian season 3 is going  to come out in february of 2023 so  hopefully this trailer isn't too far  along from being released to the general  public but that is what we saw it was  awesome and let me know how excited you  are for this trailer to finally hit and  how excited you are for the ahsoka show  and the mandalorian season three let me  know in the comments down below don't  forget to like the video and for more  star wars marvel and other awesome  videos be sure to subscribe for live  updates you can follow me on instagram  and twitter and as always thank you all  so much for watching woof  [Music]
 

